    {
      "id": "claim_78283d27dd104364aae779cfe77824a3",
      "statement": "celld is an alpha and is not safe for hostile multi-tenant use; security fixes apply to the latest release only. One fleet runs one application and celld trusts the application code, the fleet nodes, and the operators.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L3-L11",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:76ff70dbe3e47d7eac1f5a5569e9c2b6a098b44edbd9ea2ed0a49a7fdf4e8515:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1c34fc72d3924131a8075e31da137377",
      "statement": "celld opens two HTTP listeners: the public worker listener reserves only `/.well-known/celld/health`, while the internal listener serves the peer protocol and the operator API and does not pass an unknown path to the Worker (returns 404).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L20-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b099061c8fa15fa2e04fc6afb2324276da228c3619720bf990f24df2ef85ea63:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c44910fd79a34b9997dab745f43ac521",
      "statement": "An explicit advertised address requires an explicit internal-listener addressaine, and an explicit non-loopback public listener without an explicit internal listener is rejected; these checks prevent an obsolete one-listener configuration.",
